# Project Context: Marginalia

## Overview & Vision
* **App Name:** Marginalia
* **Concept:** A literary, calm, and distraction-free writing workbench designed around the philosophy: *"A website that lets you do the writing, while guiding your memory."*
* **Core Philosophy:** Serves both "Planners" (who build out characters/world details beforehand) and "Pantsers" (who write freely as the story emerges).
* **Aesthetic & Mood:** Rainy-day literary comfort. Low cognitive load, serif-driven typography, soft paper textures, and ambient background animations.

---

## Current Architecture & Tech Stack (V1)
* **Format:** Single-file application (`index.html`) combining HTML5, embedded CSS, and vanilla JS.
* **Storage:** Client-side `localStorage` (Sandboxed mock login, settings, books, and entities).
* **Typography:** `Lora` (Serif for titles/headings/literary elements), `Karla` (Sans-serif for UI chrome and controls).
* **Color Palette:**
  * Background: Rain-window grey-blue (`#E4E7E6`)
  * Cards: Warm paper-cream (`#F6F3EC`)
  * Text: Deep ink (`#2B302C`)
  * Accent: Muted slate (`#5C7380`)
  * Active States: Soft moss (`#7C8B6F`)

---

## Key Features & UI Workflows Implemented

### 1. Authentication & Testing Gate
* Mock login/signup form (email + password saved in `localStorage`).
* **Temporary Testing Feature:** A clearly marked "FOR TESTING" admin bypass button to jump directly into the app as "Admin (testing)".

### 2. The Shelf / Library (Homepage)
* Displays book projects formatted like book spines/covers.
* **Hover State:** Cards grow slightly on hover. Shows image cover + title below.
* **Dimensions:** Book covers expect `400 x 600px` (portrait).
* **New Book Flow:** "Start a new book" opens a modal asking for Title, optional Cover Upload, and initial Theme choice.
* **Card Expansion:** Clicking a book grows that exact card in-place to fill the screen (no modal popup), transitioning into the project workspace.
* **Two-Step Deletion Guardrail:**
  * Step 1: *"Delete this book? Everything inside it will be deleted with it."*
  * Step 2: *"Are you positive? There's no undo."*

### 3. Themes & Ambient Aesthetics (11 Themes)
* **Themes:** Rainy & Quiet (Default), Fantasy, Mystery, Thriller, Noir, Sci-Fi, Horror, Romance, Historical, Western, Cozy.
* Each theme includes custom Light and Dark modes, distinct palette accents, and subtle ambient animations (e.g., rain streaks, floating embers, drifting fog, rising data).
* **Theme Switching:** Selectable per-book at creation or globally via the sidebar footer.

### 4. Project Workspace & Side Navigation
* **Navbar Layout:** Collapsible side panel (toggles between expanded view with text labels and a slim icon rail view).
* **Navigation Items:** Top item is the current Book Title, followed by sub-cards: Chapters, Scenes, Characters, Locations, Items, Brain Dump.
* **Resume Banner:** Detects the single most recent save across all categories and displays a "Resume where you left off" banner (e.g., *"Chapter: Ch. 13 — 2h ago"*).

### 5. Writing Canvas (Chapters & Scenes)
* **Sub-Cards:** "Add a Scene" sits directly after "Add a Chapter".
* **Rich Text Toolbar:** Built with `document.execCommand` (paragraph styles, font families, text sizes, bold/italic/underline/strikethrough, text color, alignment, bullet/numbered lists, undo/redo, clear formatting).
* **Entity Live Match Sidebar (V1):**
  * As the user types, the editor scans text in real time against stored character, location, and item names.
  * **Matched Entity Cards:** Dynamically display in a right-hand sidebar (PC) or bottom draggable drawer (Mobile).
  * Filter chips available: All / Characters / Locations / Items.
  * Click any matched card to open its editor.

### 6. Entity Data Templates & Image Lightbox

#### Image Lightbox Protocol
* Reference images auto-resize down to max `800 x 800px` on upload.
* Thumbnails scale proportionally (max ~84px).
* **Custom Enlarge Hover:** Hovering shows a dark scrim with a diamond-flower icon (`✦`) and text *"Click to enlarge"*.
* **Lightbox Animation:** Snappy, crisp scale-up animation (~0.3s bounce) to full screen, click anywhere to shrink back down.

#### Data Templates
* **Character Template:** Reference Images (800x800 square hint) → Name, Role in Story, Goal, Age/Sex (side-by-side), Physical Description, Typical Attire, Personality, Occupation, Habits/Mannerisms, Background, Internal Conflicts, External Conflicts, Tags (items carried, race/regime, origin, comma-separated), Additional Notes.
* **Location Template:** Reference Images → Name of Setting, Location, Role in Story, Related Characters, Season/Weather, Unique Features, Description, Sights, Sounds, Smells, Additional Notes.
* **Item Template:** Reference Images → Name of Item, Point in Story → *[Grouped Description: Looks, Sounds, Effects, Potential Weaknesses]* → *[Grouped Origin: Who designed it? Why?]* → Additional Notes.
* **Brain Dump:** Single running continuous text space per book.

